            <ArticleTitle>Detection of Palmaz-Schatz stent by ultrafast CT.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>128-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of Palmaz-Schatz stent in the anterior descending coronary artery in a patient in whom restenosis occurred repeatedly after balloon angioplasty. The location of the stent was confirmed by ultrafast CT. The Palmaz-Schatz stent is barely visible by fluoroscopy and confirmation of its location by fluoroscopy is difficult after failure of stent delivery. However, ultrafast CT enabled the clear detection of a Palmaz-Schatz stent without artifacts and may be valuable in confirming its location.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
